#title: SAB-derived rectangular pyramidal horn with a virtual waveguide feed

## Geometry reconstructed from the current horn.sab (ACIS 34, CST dimensions
## in mm):
##   straight-guide length:       30.0
##   straight inner aperture:     24.0 x 10.0
##   straight outer aperture:     26.0 x 12.0
##   flare length:               228.0
##   mouth inner aperture:       110.0 x 80.0
##   mouth outer aperture:       112.0353 x 82.0234
##   total horn length:          258.0
## The new SAB has 1 mm walls at the throat. Its RF-critical inner surface and
## its outer mouth both snap naturally to this 1 mm grid, so a connected
## one-cell-thick PEC shell represents it without the impractical 0.5 mm mesh.

#domain: 0.152 0.122 0.310
#dx_dy_dz: 0.001 0.001 0.001
#time_window: 25e-9
#pml_cells: 12

## Place the SAB z=0 back aperture at z=20 mm. The 30 mm straight section ends
## at z=50 mm and the horn mouth is at z=278 mm. Four boxes per z cell form a
## closed rectangular PEC ring. Nearest-cell snapping keeps the analytic flare
## error at or below 0.5 mm while retaining a leak-free staircase shell.
#python:
dl = 1e-3
centre_x_cells = 76
centre_y_cells = 61
back_z_cell = 20
flare_z_cell = 50
mouth_z_cell = 278


def emit_box(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1):
    print(
        "#box: "
        f"{x0 * dl:.6f} {y0 * dl:.6f} {z0 * dl:.6f} "
        f"{x1 * dl:.6f} {y1 * dl:.6f} {z1 * dl:.6f} pec n"
    )


def emit_ring(x_lower, x_upper, y_lower, y_upper, z_lower, z_upper):
    emit_box(x_lower - 1, y_lower - 1, z_lower, x_lower, y_upper + 1, z_upper)
    emit_box(x_upper, y_lower - 1, z_lower, x_upper + 1, y_upper + 1, z_upper)
    emit_box(x_lower, y_lower - 1, z_lower, x_upper, y_lower, z_upper)
    emit_box(x_lower, y_upper, z_lower, x_upper, y_upper + 1, z_upper)


## Straight feed section. The new 24 x 10 mm throat and its 1 mm PEC wall are
## represented exactly on the grid.
straight_x_lower = centre_x_cells - 12
straight_x_upper = centre_x_cells + 12
straight_y_lower = centre_y_cells - 5
straight_y_upper = centre_y_cells + 5
emit_ring(
    straight_x_lower,
    straight_x_upper,
    straight_y_lower,
    straight_y_upper,
    back_z_cell,
    flare_z_cell,
)

## Pyramidal flare. Each one-cell z slab is a hollow PEC ring whose inner
## half-widths interpolate from 12 x 5 mm to 55 x 40 mm. Rounding the analytic
## inner wall to the nearest cell also puts the final outer ring at 112 x 82 mm,
## within 0.024 mm of the SAB outer-mouth dimensions.
flare_cells = mouth_z_cell - flare_z_cell
for z_cell in range(flare_z_cell, mouth_z_cell):
    fraction = (z_cell + 1 - flare_z_cell) / flare_cells
    half_x = 12.0 + fraction * (55.0 - 12.0)
    half_y = 5.0 + fraction * (40.0 - 5.0)
    x_lower = round(centre_x_cells - half_x)
    x_upper = round(centre_x_cells + half_x)
    y_lower = round(centre_y_cells - half_y)
    y_upper = round(centre_y_cells + half_y)
    emit_ring(x_lower, x_upper, y_lower, y_upper, z_cell, z_cell + 1)
#end_python:

## Port 1 lies inside the uniform straight section and launches the dominant
## mode toward +z. Its source is moved into a separately terminated auxiliary
## guide, allowing the physical horn and port aperture to sit inside a closed
## NTFF surface.
##
## The eigenmode band bounds the automatic excitation and retains only the five
## modal DFT bins that coincide with the requested far-field frequencies. Modal
## S-parameter output is not retained or used by this validation.
#eigenmode_band: horn_excitation_band 8e9 12e9 5
## The automatic modal-anchor candidates cover the requested band and the
## significant spectrum of the automatic excitation waveform, including guard
## candidates across its transition regions. Candidate validity, propagation,
## reference selection, and any fallback are resolved independently for each
## port and mode. Non-propagating candidates can serve as monitor references but
## are excluded from source and propagating-power interpolation. Modal-field
## plotting is disabled because its diagnostic mosaics are not needed here.
#eigenmode_port: 1 0.064 0.056 0.025 0.088 0.066 0.025 + 1 auto n
#virtual_waveguide: 1 21 12 6
#eigenmode_excitation: 1 1 auto y

## Closed six-face Huygens box. It encloses the complete physical horn and its
## virtual aperture, remains in free space, and stays outside the domain PML.
#ntff_surface: 0.016 0.016 0.016 0.136 0.106 0.286 horn_surface
#ntff_frequency: horn_surface horn_ntff 8e9 9e9 10e9 11e9 12e9 rectangular

## Complete 1-degree principal-plane cuts. In the gprMax spherical convention,
## phi={0,180} covers the two halves of the xz plane and phi={90,270} covers
## the two halves of the yz plane; theta spans +z through -z inclusively.
#ntff_far_field_array: 0 180 1 0 180 180 horn_ntff xz_plane Etheta Ephi radiation_intensity directivity_dbi
#ntff_far_field_array: 0 180 1 90 270 180 horn_ntff yz_plane Etheta Ephi radiation_intensity directivity_dbi

## No #ntff_antenna_ports association is made because this comparison reports
## directivity rather than gain or realized gain. Field,
## radiation-intensity, and directivity outputs remain available.

#geometry_view: 0 0 0 0.152 0.122 0.310 0.001 0.001 0.001 horn_antenna_geometry n
